<title>USA: Interlake nets $85 mln from sale of unit.</title>
<headline>Interlake nets $85 mln from sale of unit.</headline>
<dateline>LISLE, Ill. 1996-10-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>Interlake Corp said Friday it has completed the sale of its packaging businesses to Samuel Manu-Tech Inc and expects to net about $85 million in after-tax proceeds.  </p>
<p>Interlake, which designs and sells products for material handling, automotive and aerospace industries, said it will use the proceeds to repay debt, with some funds possibly being used for one or two pending acquisitions.</p>
<p>Etobicke, Ontario-based Samuel Manu-Tech manufactures and sells steel strapping.</p>
<p>Interlake stock was down 1/8 at 3-3/4.</p>
<p>--Reuters Chicago newsdesk, 312-408-8787</p>
